**Read:** [Supply Chain Resilience: Guide for Water and Wastewater Utilities — EPA](../sources/Chemical-Supply-Resilience-EPA.lingua#r_2NVE96BRQ8Q3WYFP2ZQ3NTE11F), the complete guide and cases; [Methanol Safe Handling Manual — Methanol Institute](../sources/Methanol-Safe-Handling-Manual.lingua#r_01VD6M07PMPE9J0W00Z9KD5WC0), complete incident investigation, management-of-change and readiness sections; [Oxygen Pipeline and Piping Systems — EIGA Doc 13/20](../sources/Oxygen-Pipeline-and-Piping-Systems-EIGA.lingua#r_7BBE969N5JQJES1KG9AKNBEZBV), complete relevant requalification, commissioning and operating methods; [Supply chain management for the process industry — Songsong Liu](../sources/Process-Industry-Supply-Chain-Management-Liu.lingua#r_5W74Q34MKEJAWVS30JV4QH01YQ), complete relevant dynamic/uncertain planning chapters.

For a chosen interruption, draw the sequence from detection through restored qualified delivery. Include isolating suspect stock, finding the cause, obtaining resources, repairing/replacing equipment, qualifying an alternate, transport, receiving analysis and communication. Distinguish restored nominal throughput from demonstrated accepted supply at the user.

Develop a case with an actual public disruption report and product-specific technical methods. Identify what was observed, reported by participants, inferred and proposed. Compare a temporary workaround with returning the original route to service. A temporary material or component may require different operating conditions and ongoing checks.

Calculate inventory and service through the recovery period, including partial deliveries, demand changes and release delays. Assess personnel, analytical and equipment capacity as well as the main chemical. Preserve a decision chronology with uncertainty and alternatives; explain what observations would trigger revision. After recovery, compare actual and predicted quantities/times and use the discrepancy to improve the model. A simulated restoration or literature reconstruction should describe its limits while still producing a defensible technical understanding of the linked system.

**Continue:** [Account for the human work behind reliable chemical supply](../operation/People-knowledge-and-organisations-that-keep-materials-moving.lingua#r_59R4FQW1E554XQYJ3BTEY8ASTA).

